# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights.
#
# weights/ is where `scripts/weights/collect_weights.sh` assembles the release
# bundle, and it is deliberately untracked: the two exact-13-mer checkpoints are
# 8 GiB each because 99.99% of their parameters are the embedding table. They are
# distributed through the archive named in weights/README.md, which stays tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
weights/*
!weights/README.md
!weights/ZENODO.md
!weights/.gitkeep

*.pt
*.ckpt
*.pth
*.safetensors

# Vocabularies and their cached lookup tables. vocab_13mer.txt is 480 MB and its
# int32 lookup table is 256 MiB; both are rebuildable and are distributed with
# the data, not the code. See docs/DATA.md.
vocab_*.txt
*.table_k*.npy

# Reads, reference genomes, label tables. All of it is data, none of it is code.
*.fa
*.fna
*.fasta
*.fq
*.fastq
*.fastq.gz
*.fq.gz
*.tsv
*.npz
!docs/**/*.tsv
# The prediction arrays behind docs/RESULTS.md's abundance-vs-detection
# table. Kept (preds + labels only, ~220 KB each) because they are what
# makes that table checkable without re-running a 2.1B-parameter model,
# and because two 100K pools agree on 8% of labels -- the stored label
# vector is the only thing that says which pool a row is on.
!docs/assets/*.npz
!examples/*.fa
!examples/*.tsv
!tests/fixtures/*.json
!tests/fixtures/*.npz
!reproduction/**/*.npz
!reproduction/**/*.tsv

# Run outputs: KF_OUT should point outside the repo, but catch it if it does not.
runs/
outputs/
out/
eval_*/
training_history.csv
*.log

# Archives
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.zip

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
.conda/

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Experiment trackers
wandb/
lightning_logs/

# Operational handoff briefs for agents on the training machines. They name
# internal cluster paths and an account name -- useful on those boxes, useless to
# anyone else -- so they stay on disk and out of the repository.
docs/agent_prompts/

# Downloaded inference bundles and derived training indexes
models/
*.idx.npy
*.idx.npy.meta.json

# machine-specific source paths for scripts/fetch and scripts/weights
scripts/local_paths.sh
